 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "A lamp lights on «الحق» and undraws at «وتكتمون» (the truth concealed); night_day for the morning-and-evening ploy; a lamp for «الهدى هدى الله». 73:1-6 is attributed («قال بعضهم لبعض») so it is never read as advice to the viewer. 73:12-21 is not glossed: its parsing differs between the tafsirs. STAGING v4: 70-71: the People of the Book (k) in a town at dusk: they shake their heads on 70:4 (they deny), read their book on 70:8 (they witness it, Al-Muyassar: it is in their books), speak on 71:4 (mixing truth with falsehood) and turn their backs on 71:7 (concealing); a lamp on the truth undraws on 71:7. 72-73: «طائفة» = only the faction (f, a tight group) plots and speaks among themselves (As-Sa'di: قال بعضهم لبعض) while the rest (o) stay still; they point at the believers (b) on 72:10; the plot is only spoken, never acted out (the verse reports their words). 73:12-21 (parsing differs): camera only. Light plate on «الهدى» (73:9) and sparkle on the believers (Al-Muyassar: those who believe) on 73:28; geometric only on the Name (73:26)."
 },
